kwin 6.8: hand a fullscreen client's wl_shm buffer to the host as it is

Direct scanout in kwin needs a DRM scanout device and a dmabuf client buffer,
so a kwin nested over wl_shm (kwin-6.8-software-shm-presentation.patch) composes
every frame through llvmpipe, even when one opaque surface covers the screen.

Let an output layer say it accepts shm scanout, which the Wayland backend's layers
do when they present through wl_shm, and let the compositor and the scene's
candidate search take a client's wl_shm buffer for such a layer: only one covering
the whole output, as an overlay would merely move the composing to the host. The
buffer is attached to the layer's subsurface like kwin's own frames, in the
formats the host takes, and the client keeps it until the host releases it, as
with dmabuf scanout. Its pool may hold the buffer at an offset, so the host-side
pool is sized to include it. When kwin composes again, the first frame repaints
everything, as kwin's own buffers no longer show what the host last displayed,
and the layer reports the presented item so clients get their frame feedback.

Applies to kwin 6.8.x after kwin-6.8-software-shm-presentation.patch.

